A||N||11||grinthock||Which Dist plug is cyl 1?  Quick pls.  work in prog||||1||
Z||000000||grinthock||08-29-2001||06:25 PM||||hey guys/gals thanks for the quick responses!  I am trying to get the car back togeather, I was a moron and ripped off all the wires (angry fiero rage!)  and didn't mark which one is cyl 1.<P>How do I know which plug on the dist is cyl 1?  Also what is the correct firing order?<P>I need to know because I got a set of taylor custom wires and want to make them perfect.<P>Thanks<P>Justin<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroworldbanner.gif"> </A> <BR>Fieroworld!  Home of my 87 GT and 85 GT<BR>Justin C.<BR>Engineer, Designer and<BR>Technical Trainer for Nortel Networks Business Products.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Joe Torma||08-29-2001||06:32 PM||||It depends on where you have the distributor set at for #1.  Bring #1 up on the compression stroke to TDC.  This will show you where you need to put the wire.  <BR>Otherwise you can reset the deistributor...set the rotor to point twords #1 cylender then put #1 wire there when you put the cap on.<P>Joe<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig.gif">   <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 08-29-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000002||grinthock||08-29-2001||08:37 PM||||To reset the distributor I would have to redo the timing... Would rather not.<P><BR>what's the best way to line up TDC on CYL 1 Compression Stroke?||||reg||1
Z||000003||grinthock||08-29-2001||08:45 PM||||I almost forgot, the book I have doesn't specify what the firing order is (I know it's 123456) but where are those cyl's.<P><BR>I was told<P>        FIREWALL<P>    1     3     5<BR>  <BR>    2     4     6<P>      TRUNK||||reg||1
Z||000004||Joe Torma||08-29-2001||08:47 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by grinthock:<BR><B>I almost forgot, the book I have doesn't specify what the firing order is (I know it's 123456) but where are those cyl's.<P><BR>I was told<P>        FIREWALL<P>    1     3     5<BR>  <BR>    2     4     6<P>      TRUNK</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>AK!! No!<BR>FIREWALL<BR> 642<BR> 531<BR>TRUNK<P>That will really ^%$# things up!<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Joe Torma||08-29-2001||08:52 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by grinthock:<BR><B>To reset the distributor I would have to redo the timing... Would rather not.what's the best way to line up TDC on CYL 1 Compression Stroke?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Wad up some paper towel in an earplug kinda configuration and stuff it in the #1 plug hole--tightly, so it wont fall in or out.  Turn the engine by hand clockwise until it pops out or you can hear air escaping.  Bring the timing mark up to the 0 on the tab.  There ya go.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||grinthock||08-29-2001||09:02 PM||||Ok, so do I just put a wratchet on the nut on the big pulley and turn clockwise till it lines up, I can't see the markings, so I will just watch for the compression stroke on 1.  Then I have to pull the dist cap and see where the rotor is sitting?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Slammed Fiero||08-29-2001||09:09 PM||||It doesn't matter which way the plug wires go on. Just make the long ones go to the plugs that are furthest away.<P>Works great for me , car idles a little erratically though.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000008||grinthock||08-29-2001||09:10 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B>It doesn't matter which way the plug wires go on. Just make the long ones go to the plugs that are furthest away.<P>Works great for me , car idles a little erratically though.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>JM </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif">  You are just hilarious tonight JM!  Hope the car is doin well!<P><P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroworldbanner.gif"> </A> <BR>Fieroworld!  Home of my 87 GT and 85 GT<BR>Justin C.<BR>Engineer, Designer and<BR>Technical Trainer for Nortel Networks Business Products.||||reg||1
Z||000009||skitime||08-29-2001||09:13 PM||||Grint, you didn't believe when I told you all this stuff did you.  Hey, I will sit on chat for a while if you still need help.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/chat/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/chat/</A> <P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by skitime (edited 08-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||Joe Torma||08-29-2001||09:41 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by grinthock:<BR><B>Ok, so do I just put a wratchet on the nut on the big pulley and turn clockwise till it lines up, I can't see the markings, so I will just watch for the compression stroke on 1.  Then I have to pull the dist cap and see where the rotor is sitting?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes, just pop off the cap to see where your #1 is.  You will also need to find your timing mark to make sure it is at 0.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||2birds||08-29-2001||11:42 PM||||When you figure out which of the three slots is the balancer is the one for cylinder #1 at TDC, make sure you mark it with some liquid paper or paint so you can find it easier the next time you need to find it.<P>For what it's worth, my #1 plug wire goes at the 1 o'clock position, if you consider the flat side of the cap to be a horizontal plane from 5 to 7 o'clock.<P>Don't forget to go clockwise...||||reg||1
